{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And if you refuse.</b> And if you are a refuser. <b>מאן.</b> Like מְמָאֵן, מְסָרֵב — rather, a person is called by the name of the action, like ״שָׁלֵו״ (Job 16), ״שָׁקֵט״ (Judges 18), ״סַר וְזָעֵף״ (I Kings 20)." "<b>Will smite all your border.</b> Striking. And so every term of מַגֵּפָה is not a term of death but a term of blow, and so ״וְנָגְפוּ אִשָּׁה הָרָה״ (Exodus 21) — not a term of death, and so ״וּבְטֶרֶם יִתְנַגְּפוּ רַגְלֵיכֶם״ (Jeremiah 13), ״פֶּן תִּגֹּף בָּאֶבֶן רַגְלֶךָ״ (Psalms 91), ״וּלְאֶבֶן נֶגֶף״ (Isaiah 8)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:02.715153291Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}